## Serena-First for Code Navigation

**When navigating, understanding, or searching code, ALWAYS try Serena first.** Only fall back to Grep/Read when Serena cannot help (non-code content, string literals, config files).

| Task                               | Use This                               | NOT This                   |
| ---------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| Find a function/class/variable     | `serena` find_symbol                   | Grep                       |
| Find who calls/references a symbol | `serena` find_referencing_symbols      | Grep                       |
| Understand a file's structure      | `serena` get_symbols_overview          | Read (entire file)         |
| Get a class's methods/properties   | `serena` find_symbol depth:1           | Read (entire file)         |
| Get type info or signature         | `serena` find_symbol include_info:true | Read + manual parsing      |
| Read a specific function body      | `serena` find_symbol include_body:true | Read (entire file)         |
| Rename impact analysis             | `serena` find_referencing_symbols      | Grep (misses aliased refs) |
| Search for non-code strings/logs   | Grep                                   | —                          |
| Read config/JSON/markdown files    | Read                                   | —                          |

## Prohibited Patterns

1. Using Grep to find functions, classes, or variable definitions when `serena` is available
2. Using Read to understand a file's structure instead of `serena` get_symbols_overview
3. Using Grep for "who calls X" instead of `serena` find_referencing_symbols
